# Where `.claude/optmem/to-obsidian` writes the memory note.
#
# Copy this file to `obsidian.conf` (same directory) and set VAULT for THIS
# machine. That file is gitignored: the vault lives at a different path on
# the Windows desktop than on the Mac, so the path must never be committed.
# $OBSIDIAN_VAULT / $OBSIDIAN_NOTE in the environment override this file.
#
# VAULT is the vault root — the folder Obsidian opens, the one containing
# `.obsidian/`. NOTE is relative to it.

# --- macOS ---------------------------------------------------------------
# VAULT=/Users/you/Documents/MyVault
# An iCloud-synced vault lives under:
# VAULT=/Users/you/Library/Mobile Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/MyVault

# --- Windows -------------------------------------------------------------
# Forward slashes work fine in Python on Windows, and avoid escaping pain:
# VAULT=C:/Users/you/Documents/MyVault
# Under Git Bash or WSL a POSIX path works too:
# VAULT=/c/Users/you/Documents/MyVault

# --- The note ------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to "permanent claude memories/EXSTO-ERGO-SUM.md". The folder is
# created if missing. The script will not overwrite a note it did not write.
# NOTE=permanent claude memories/EXSTO-ERGO-SUM.md
